    "passage": "<div class=\"ttl\">Passage 1 (Questions 1&ndash;6)</div>\n<p>DNA double-strand breaks (DSBs) represent the most cytotoxic form of genomic lesions. Eukaryotic cells deploy two distinct pathways to resolve DSBs: homologous recombination (HR) and non-homologous end joining (NHEJ). HR operates primarily during the S and G2 phases of the cell cycle, utilizing an undamaged sister chromatid as a repair template to ensure high-fidelity, error-free restoration of the original sequence. The pathway initiates when the MRN endonuclease complex (Mre11-Rad50-Nbs1) resects broken DNA ends 5'-to-3' to yield extended 3' single-stranded DNA (ssDNA) tails. BRCA1 coordinates cell-cycle checkpoint signaling and CtIP recruitment, while BRCA2 directs the displacement of replication protein A (RPA) by Rad51 recombinase. Rad51 nucleoprotein filaments then invade the homologous sister duplex, catalyzing strand invasion and forming Holliday junctions that are resolved into intact duplexes.</p>\n<p>In contrast, NHEJ functions throughout all cell cycle stages, particularly during G0/G1 when sister chromatids are absent. NHEJ is initiated by the Ku70/Ku80 heterodimer, which rings the broken blunt DNA ends and recruits the catalytic subunit of DNA-dependent protein kinase (DNA-PKcs). The Artemis endonuclease processes non-matching damaged termini prior to direct ligation by DNA Ligase IV and XRCC4. Because end processing frequently deletes or inserts nucleotides, NHEJ is intrinsically error-prone and can generate chromosomal translocations.</p>\n<p>Poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase 1 (PARP1) detects single-strand breaks (SSBs) and coordinates base excision repair. When PARP1 is inhibited pharmacologically by olaparib, unrepaired SSBs encounter advancing replication forks during S phase, causing fork collapse into one-ended DSBs. While HR-proficient cells resolve these replication-associated DSBs seamlessly, HR-deficient cells (such as <em>BRCA1</em>- or <em>BRCA2</em>-mutated cancer cells) are forced to rely on toxic, aberrant end-joining or suffer catastrophic mitotic death—a therapeutic principle termed synthetic lethality.</p>\n<p>Researchers evaluated four human triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC) cell lines: wild-type (WT, HR-proficient), <em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> (HR-deficient), <em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> with Ku70 knockdown (Ku70-KD), and <em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> with Rad51 overexpression (Rad51-OE). Cells were treated with 1 &mu;M olaparib or vehicle for 48 hours. Double-strand breaks were quantified via phosphorylated histone &gamma;-H2AX nuclear foci, HR competence was evaluated by Rad51 focus formation, and cell survival was measured by clonogenic colony assay (Table 1).</p>\n<table class=\"tbl\">\n  <caption>Table 1 Arcuate DDR markers, chromosomal aberrations, and clonogenic survival across breast cancer cell lines</caption>\n  <thead>\n    <tr><th>Genotype &amp; Treatment</th><th>&gamma;-H2AX Foci / Cell</th><th>Rad51 Foci / Cell</th><th>Aberrations / Metaphase</th><th>Clonogenic Survival (%)</th></tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>WT + Vehicle</td><td>3.2 &plusmn; 0.4</td><td>1.1 &plusmn; 0.2</td><td>0.08 &plusmn; 0.02</td><td>100.0 &plusmn; 4.2</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>WT + Olaparib</td><td>18.5 &plusmn; 1.6</td><td>16.8 &plusmn; 1.4</td><td>0.22 &plusmn; 0.04</td><td>92.4 &plusmn; 3.8</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> + Vehicle</td><td>6.4 &plusmn; 0.7</td><td>0.8 &plusmn; 0.1</td><td>0.45 &plusmn; 0.06</td><td>88.5 &plusmn; 3.5</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> + Olaparib</td><td>42.1 &plusmn; 3.5</td><td>1.4 &plusmn; 0.2</td><td>4.86 &plusmn; 0.42</td><td>4.6 &plusmn; 0.8</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> + Ku70-KD + Olaparib</td><td>39.8 &plusmn; 3.1</td><td>1.2 &plusmn; 0.2</td><td>2.14 &plusmn; 0.25</td><td>28.3 &plusmn; 2.4</td></tr>\n    <tr><td><em>BRCA1</em><sup>&minus;/&minus;</sup> + Rad51-OE + Olaparib</td><td>21.3 &plusmn; 1.9</td><td>14.5 &plusmn; 1.3</td><td>0.68 &plusmn; 0.08</td><td>74.2 &plusmn; 3.6</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
